====================================================
UAF ice radar flicker detection code base


==========================
OVERVIEW

This tool creates "flicker" images from a specified squence of sea ice radar (SIR) images 
Flickering is defined by calculating the pixel-wise normalized standard deviation of 
of pixels values in the image sequence.

Normalized normalized standard deviation is defined as:

	sigma* = sigma / sqrt(b_mean)

where:

	sigma = pixel-wise standard deviation of pixel brightness
	p_mean = pixel-wise mean brightness

A pixel is consider to be flickering if sigma* > sigma_flick (typically = 1)

If a pixel is not flickering, it is considered to be steady.


==========================
CODE SUMMARY

=== PRIMARY FUNCTIONS ===

--- Flicker image generator
		SIR_flickerlyzer(sirlist, varargin)
		
    This function takes a sequence of SIR images and feeds them into a first-in-first-out stack of N images
    A flicker image is produced for every complete stack (i.e., 1 + sequence_length - N)
    Optionally, this tool creates a mean image for each stack as well.
                                         


--- Flickerlyzer Wrapper
        SIR_flickerlyzer_wrapper

  	A example wrapper function for running the Flickerlyzer on a long series of SIR images
  	

--- Flickerlyzer Demo
        SIR_flickerlyzer_demo

  	A simple function that serves as a wrapper for running the code base with the test data included in this repository

   
=== ANCILIARY FUNCTIONS ===


--- Flicker filter: 
		fflick = SIR_flicker_filter(flickimg, rad)

    This function applies a sequence of opening and closing operations to remove small regions of flickering steady pixels from flicker image

--- Custom color ramp generator
        cmap = generatecolorramp(coldefs, Ncols)

    Tool for making linear color ramps between specified colors.
    Used for making the split color ramps for flickering and steady pixels


==========================
DEMO DATA

Test data for this code base are contained in the "TestData" folder, which contains following:

--- Cropped
	A folder containing cropped SIR images, produced as a "raw" data product from each SIR system
	Images are organized into subfolder first by year and then calendar day (i.e., yyyy/yyyymmdd)

---	FlickerImages
	A folder containing flicker images output by running SIR_flickerlyzer_demo

---	StackMeans
	A folder containing stack mean images output by running SIR_flickerlyzer_demo

